# Trigger Phrase Registry

Centralized registry of trigger phrases used by `@agent-orchestrator.mdc` for routing user intent to appropriate helpers.

## Purpose

Maintain single source of truth for trigger phrases to prevent drift and routing ambiguity across orchestrator and task rules.

## Trigger Categories

### Feature Implementation

```yaml
triggers: ["implement", "add feature", "create feature", "build", "work on", "start on"]
```

### Bug Fixes

```yaml
triggers: ["fix bug", "fix error", "fix issue", "bug in", "error in", "broken", "debug"]
```

### Maintenance/Refactoring

```yaml
triggers: ["refactor", "clean up", "organize", "optimize", "improve", "restructure"]
```

### Testing

```yaml
triggers: ["write test", "add test", "test", "run test", "verify", "validate"]
```

### Linting/Formatting

```yaml
triggers: ["lint", "format", "fix formatting", "run linter", "clean code"]
```

### Documentation

```yaml
triggers: ["update docs", "write documentation", "add comments", "document"]
```

### Research/Investigation

```yaml
triggers: ["research", "investigate", "analyze", "explore", "find", "understand", "how does"]
```

## Usage

Orchestrator and task rules should reference these canonical lists instead of maintaining their own copies. Example:

```markdown
If user input matches triggers from @triggers.mdc#bug-fixes:
- Route to @helper-bugfix.mdc
```

## Maintenance

- Update this file when adding new workflow types
- Keep phrases lowercase for case-insensitive matching
- Avoid overlapping phrases between categories
- Test routing with sample inputs after changes
